---
import CaseStudy from '../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';
import walkaroundHifi from '../../assets/work/cat-inspect/walkaround-hifi.png';
import dashboardHifi from '../../assets/work/cat-inspect/dashboard-hifi.png';
import walkaroundScreen from '../../assets/work/cat-inspect/walkaround-screen.png';
import colors from '../../assets/work/cat-inspect/colors-yellow.png';
import buttons from '../../assets/work/cat-inspect/buttons-yellow-v2.png';

const sections = [
  {
    id: 'problem',
    navLabel: 'Problem',
    heading: 'Dense, paper-style forms fail when your hands are full.',
    body: [
      'Cat Inspect supports technicians and fleet managers running daily walk-arounds and safety checks on heavy machinery. Returning to an earlier version of the app at HackIllinois 2026 made its central problem obvious: it was built for a desk, not an active job site.',
      'Technicians had to pinch-to-zoom tiny inputs, retype equipment IDs outdoors in heavy gloves, and guess what to inspect first when cellular service dropped. Diagnostic accuracy relied almost entirely on an individual’s experience level rather than structured software guidance.',
    ],
    pullQuote: '“A workflow that works fine in an office breaks down the moment you’re in the rain with one hand on a machine.”',
  },
  {
    id: 'process',
    navLabel: 'Process',
    heading: 'Designing for field constraints first, AI features second.',
    body: [
      'Leading design across a 36-hour sprint, I anchored our 3-person team around environmental realities: sunlight glare, thick gloves, offline connectivity, and high time pressure.',
      'Before touching AI, we audited the baseline checklist to eliminate duplicate data entry and establish clear offline states. We then strictly scoped features around tangible friction:',
    ],
    groups: [
      {
        items: [
          {
            lead: 'Built as functional prototypes',
            text: 'Hold-to-speak voice notes and on-device computer vision that drafts defect severity.',
          },
          {
            lead: 'Scoped to the roadmap',
            text: 'Predictive failure alerts and dynamic, sensor-driven checklist ordering.',
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'decision',
    navLabel: 'Decision',
    heading: 'From sprawling forms to a high-contrast, step-by-step walk-around.',
    body: [],
    leadWithGroups: true,
    groups: [
      {
        items: [
          {
            lead: 'Frictionless Intake & Offline Clarity',
            text: 'A single machine dashboard replaces open-ended forms. Technicians scan a QR code to pull asset IDs, and a prominent sync indicator removes ambiguity around local storage. Pre-inspection gates prevent submission until safety-critical fields are complete.',
          },
          {
            lead: 'Glove-Calibrated Controls',
            text: 'Inspections now advance one component at a time. Oversized, high-contrast touch targets and a 4-state selector (Normal, Monitor, Action Required, N/A) replace tedious text input.',
          },
          {
            lead: 'Human-in-the-Loop Logging',
            text: 'Technicians can dictate notes or snap photos inline without leaving the checklist. The computer-vision integration pre-selects a defect rating, but always requires explicit technician confirmation before saving.',
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
    pullQuote: '“AI suggests the severity rating; the technician always makes the final call.”',
    images: [
      {
        src: dashboardHifi,
        alt: 'Daily Inspection dashboard for a CAT D8T Dozer showing sync status, a pre-inspection setup checklist with QR auto-fill, and walk-around progress',
        caption: 'Asset onboarding with QR auto-fill, required field gates, and clear offline sync status.',
      },
      {
        src: walkaroundScreen,
        alt: 'Guided walk-around step for a CAT D8T Dozer showing a fluid systems check, a Normal/Monitor/Action Required/N/A status selector, and hold-to-speak note and photo capture controls',
        caption: 'Single-step view featuring glove-friendly status targets and inline voice/photo capture.',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'outcome',
    navLabel: 'Outcome',
    heading: 'A rebuilt inspection flow — untested outside the team, so far.',
    body: [
      'By the end of HackIllinois 2026, the redesign moved from concept to a working high-fidelity prototype — combining the guided walk-around, structured asset dashboard, and functional prototypes for computer-vision defect drafting and voice-to-text notes.',
      'While the 36-hour sprint focused on core interaction architecture over formal user testing, the foundation is deliberately production-ready. Design tokens, high-contrast state colors, and glove-calibrated touch targets were built to standard for seamless engineering handoff.',
    ],
    images: [
      {
        src: colors,
        alt: 'Cat Inspect brand color palette: Caterpillar Yellow and Navy as brand colors, plus state colors for success, warning, and alert, and a neutral grayscale ramp',
        caption: 'Production tokens covering high-visibility contrast ratios and brand colors.',
      },
      {
        src: buttons,
        alt: 'Cat Inspect button component specification in Caterpillar Yellow and Navy, showing primary and secondary color styles, plus default, hover, and disabled variants',
        caption: 'Production component tokens covering interaction states.',
      },
    ],
    groups: [
      {
        title: 'Next Steps & Validation Priorities',
        items: [
          {
            lead: 'Field Ergonomics',
            text: 'Run usability sessions with technicians wearing heavy work gloves to evaluate tap accuracy on the status selector.',
          },
          {
            lead: 'Ambient Audio Testing',
            text: 'Benchmark voice-to-text capture against active job-site engine noise.',
          },
          {
            lead: 'Roadmap Concepts',
            text: 'Scope predictive maintenance triggers and dynamic, conditional checklists into future releases once baseline telemetry is active.',
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<CaseStudy
  title="Cat Inspect"
  slug="cat-inspect"
  dek="Redesigning Caterpillar's field inspection app for the reality of outdoor work: gloved hands, bad signal, no time to spare."
  role="Lead Product Designer"
  timeline="HackIllinois 2026"
  team="3-person team"
  skills="Field UX Design · AI-Integrated Workflows · Rapid Prototyping · Accessibility (High-Contrast, Glove-Friendly)"
  gradient="coral"
  heroImage={walkaroundHifi}
  heroImageAlt="iPhone showing the Cat Inspect pre-inspection checklist for a CAT D8T Dozer, with required fields and a Start Inspection button"
  heroMockup
  sections={sections}
  prev={{ slug: 'i-study', title: 'I-Study' }}
/>
